---
/**
 * The 404 page — added August 6, 2026, and it exists to fix a status code, not
 * to say anything.
 *
 * THE BUG IT FIXES. Cloudflare Pages falls back to serving index.html with a
 * 200 for any path it cannot match, when the deployment contains no 404.html.
 * So https://kylecovan.com/anything-at-all returned the FULL HOME PAGE and told
 * every crawler it was a real, successful page. That is a "soft 404": Google
 * reads it as one page duplicated across infinite URLs, spends crawl budget
 * confirming each one, and learns that this site's status codes cannot be
 * trusted. Reproduced on kylecovan-site.pages.dev as well as the apex, which is
 * how it was pinned on Pages' fallback rather than on a Cloudflare zone rule.
 *
 * Shipping ANY 404.html turns that fallback off — Pages serves this file with a
 * real 404 instead. That is the entire job. The words below are incidental.
 *
 * NO JSON-LD, deliberately. Every other page carries a block and verify_site.py
 * asserts exactly one on each, but that check globs `**\/index.html` and Astro
 * emits this route as `dist/404.html`, so this page is correctly outside it.
 * Structured data describes a document worth indexing; an error page is not one.
 *
 * The copy is NOT Kyle's — it is placeholder written to be replaced, and it is
 * the only text on the site not in his voice. Three short strings, no prose, so
 * that swapping them costs nothing. See handoff section 6.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Page not found — Kyle Covan"
  description="That page doesn't exist. Links to the rest of the site."
  path="/404.html"
>

  <header class="masthead-page">
    <h1>Page not found</h1>
  </header>

  <p class="lede">That page doesn't exist, or it moved.</p>

  <p class="more"><a href="/">Back to the home page</a></p>

</Base>
